          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What one usually refers to as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            is defined on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+geometry"} Lorentzian geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"} signature
            other than Lorentz.
          %p
            In
            %a{:href => "#Hul98duality"} Hull (1998)
            it is argued that there exists a web of Type II theories related by
            %strong space-
            or
            %strong time-like
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
          %p
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/nonlorentziantypesii.PNG", :width => "500px"}/
          %p
            where in particular “IIA/B” refers to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            and “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi IIA
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} IIA^*/B^*
            ” to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II%2A+string+theory"} type II* string theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi IIA
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∫
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 10
                  %mi x
                  %msqrt
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo +
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Φ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ±
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Φ
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ±
                  %msubsup
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ±
                  %msubsup
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_{IIA} = \int d^{10}x\sqrt{\vert g\vert} (e^{-2\Phi}(R+4(\partial\Phi)^2 )-(\pm e^{-2\Phi}H^2\pm G^2_2 \pm G^2_4))+\cdots
          %p
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/typeiias.PNG", :width => "500px"}/
          %p while for the Type IIB’s:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi IIA
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∫
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 10
                  %mi x
                  %msqrt
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo +
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Φ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ±
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Φ
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ±
                  %msubsup
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ±
                  %msubsup
                    %mi G
                    %mn 3
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ±
                  %msubsup
                    %mi G
                    %mn 5
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_{IIA} = \int d^{10}x\sqrt{\vert g\vert} (e^{-2\Phi}(R+4(\partial\Phi)^2 )-(\pm e^{-2\Phi}H^2\pm G^2_1 \pm G^2_3\pm G^2_5 ))+\cdots
          %p
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/typeiibs.PNG", :width => "500px"}/
          %h2#references References
          %p General:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Hull"}> Christopher Hull
                \.
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Timelike T-duality, de Sitter space, large N gauge theories and topological field theory
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9806146"} hep-th/9806146
            %li#Hul98duality
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Hull"}> Christopher Hull
                \.
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Duality and the signature of space-time
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9807127"} hep-th/9807127
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Hull"} Christopher Hull
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ramzi+Khuri"} Ramzi Khuri
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Branes, times and dualities
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9808069"} hep-th/9808069
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Hull"}> Christopher Hull
                \.
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Duality and Strings, Space and Time
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9911080"} hep-th/9911080
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitoshi+Nishino"}> Hitoshi Nishino
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"} Jim Gates
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    The
                    = succeed "-Report" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9908136"} hep-th/9908136
          %p
            On the relation between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebras
            of II and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi II
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} II^\ast
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthosymplectic+super+Lie+algebra"} orthosymplectic super Lie algebra
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔬𝔰𝔭
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 32
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{osp}(1\vert 32)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Bergshoeff"}> Eric Bergshoeff
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Antoine+Van+Proeyen"} Antoine Van Proeyen
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    The many faces of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi OSp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mn 32
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} OSp(1\vert 32)
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0003261"} hep-th/0003261
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Bergshoeff"}> Eric Bergshoeff
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Antoine+Van+Proeyen"} Antoine Van Proeyen
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    The unifying superalgebra
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi OSp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mn 32
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} OSp(1\vert 32)
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0010194"} hep-th/0010194
          %p
            The supposed branes in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi II
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} II^\ast
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                E-branes
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/E-branes"} ?
          %ul
            %li
              Somdatta Bhattacharya, Sudipta Mukherji, Shibaji Roy.
              = succeed "." do
                %em On the effective action of a space-like brane
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0308069"} hep-th/0308069
          %p
            That the boundary state for the Dirichlet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-brane"} S-brane
            constructed is a solution of type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi II
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} II^\ast
            rather than type II string theory is in:
          %ul
            %li
              Bruno Durin,
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Pioline"} Boris Pioline
              = succeed "." do
                %em Aspects of Dirichlet S-branes
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0507059"} hep-th/0507059
          %p
            The suggestion that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi II
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} II^\ast
            and its would-be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            lift may play a role in interpreting M-theory as defined on the base space of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonionic+projective+space"} octonionic projective space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}P^2
            bundle with structure group the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+Lie+group"} exceptional Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_4
            is in Remark 5, Section 2.3 of:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              \.
              = succeed "." do
                %em On the geometry of the supermultiplet in M-theory
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0909.4737"} arXiv:0909.4737
          %p
            On the relation of twisted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=2
            algebra,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/para-quaternionic+structure"} Para-quaternionic Kähler manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi II
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} II^\ast
            on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+variety"} Calabi-Yau's
          %ul
            %li
              Maxime Médevielle,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Mohaupt"} Thomas Mohaupt
              = succeed "." do
                %em Type-II Calabi-Yau compactifications, T-duality and special geometry in general spacetime signature
              = succeed "048)]" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP02(2022"} doi:10.1007/JHEP02(2022)048
